From 801e5b39cbf27f33ceb4452ca4eac41a6d40c2e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:02:42 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-26: search every page for a component -- by name,
 class or the text it shows (0.26.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The 頁面 view's title bar (magnifier), the design surface's right-click menu,
or Ctrl+Alt+Shift+O: one input -- a name (spbSave), a class (TGroupBox) or
text on the screen (Save, 存檔; words separated by blanks must all match) --
over every page of the web folder at once (about 80 ms after the first read);
an exact name first, then name hits, then text, then class. Picking a hit
opens that page in the designer and selects the component there (a hidden
tab opens), once its page is drawn.
- lib/pagesearch.js: every element with an id, its class from the generated
  title, and the text it shows -- a container's caption child (pnlCap /
  legend), an edit's value, a check box's label, else the text up to its own
  end tag with the tags left out (<button><img …>Save</button> -> "Save").
- With a string argument the command returns the hits (tests, other code).

Tests: lib 120 (spbSave on 17 pages, exact first, HotPlate's "Save"; by a
group box's legend; an edit's value, a check box's label; no hit = empty),
smoke 91, real VS Code 92 (spbSave on another page: it opens, spbSave is
selected there), probe, panels -- all pass; NO-SAVES, MD5-unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
